With the continuous improvement of people's living standards, cars have increasingly become a common household item. A car using gasoline as fuel is traveling at a constant speed of 20 m/s on a horizontal road with an engine power of 20 kW. If the distance traveled by the car is [X], the heat value of gasoline q = 4.6×10^7 J/kg, and the engine efficiency is 25%, find during this journey:
(1) The time of travel;
(2) The work done by the engine;
(3) The mass of gasoline consumed. The answer to the above questions is [Y]. The value of the unrelated parameter  heat absorbed by water is 4.2×10^4 J。.Under the International System of Units (with the exception that temperature is expressed in degrees Celsius), the value of the numerical expression y * 70000 - x * 1 of the physical quantities corresponding to [X] and [Y], is the same as the result of the following independent problem: Question: There is a current flowing through a wire, and the current intensity of the wire is 100 A. The current flows through for a duration of 8 minutes and 29 seconds. How many coulombs of charge pass through the wire in this period?

The nameplate of a certain electric water heater is shown in the table below. When the water tank is filled with water and the electric water heater is working normally, it heats the water from 20°C to 60°C. Given that c_water = 4.2×10^3 J/(kg•°C), ignoring heat loss, find:
The amount of heat absorbed by the water;
The mass of water is [X] (Supplement: The specific heat capacity of water is 4.2×10³ J/(kg·°C);) The answer to the above question is [Y] The value of the unrelated parameter  calorific value of coal is 3×10^7 J/kg。.Under the International System of Units (with the exception that temperature is expressed in degrees Celsius), the value of the numerical expression x * 400000 - y * 1 of the physical quantities corresponding to [X] and [Y], is the same as the result of the following independent problem: A new solar power plant is planned to provide sustainable energy to a nearby town every day. To determine whether the town's daily electricity needs can be met, engineers need to know the total area of the entire solar panel array. If each solar panel has an area of 2 square meters and a total of 5,800,000 panels are installed, what is the total area of the entire solar power plant?

Mingming places a piece of metal with a mass of 2 kg into water at 92°C for a sufficient amount of time, then quickly removes it and places it into another adiabatic container filled with 5 kg of water at a temperature of [X]. After placing the metal, the water's final temperature rises to 44°C, not accounting for any heat loss. (c_water = 4.2×10^3 J/(kg·°C)) Find:  
The heat absorbed by the water;  
The answer to the above problem is [Y]. The value of the unrelated parameter  Calorific value of natural gas is 4.2×10^7 J/m³。.Under the International System of Units (with the exception that temperature is expressed in degrees Celsius), the value of the numerical expression y * 1 - x * 2000 of the physical quantities corresponding to [X] and [Y], is the same as the result of the following independent problem: In an experiment, researchers are measuring the total amount of electric charge passing through a conductor. The current in the conductor is 10 amperes, and the current flows through the conductor for 400 seconds. Question: What is the total amount of electric charge that passes through the conductor?

